1
00:00:10,205 --> 00:00:15,160
I honestly can't believe Ms. Mondo
is your grandma, Mr. Seo.

2
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:19,093
More importantly, why did you
suddenly come back?

3
00:00:19,093 --> 00:00:24,213
Well, this was originally my house.

4
00:00:24,213 --> 00:00:25,637
No, no...

5
00:00:25,637 --> 00:00:29,685
You haven't been back once
since I left Merry.

6
00:00:29,685 --> 00:00:31,500
True.

7
00:00:33,705 --> 00:00:38,125
This character is cute.
Is everything going well?

8
00:00:38,125 --> 00:00:42,101
It's very popular with middle-aged
corporate guys.

9
00:00:42,101 --> 00:00:46,527
But we haven't been able to
win over very many younger fans.

10
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:49,468
What about that? Aren't you entering?

11
00:00:49,468 --> 00:00:50,969
Oh, right, that.

12
00:00:50,969 --> 00:00:53,148
The All-Japan Character Grand Prix.

13
00:00:53,148 --> 00:00:56,857
In the character business world,
it's the biggest event of the year.

14
00:00:56,857 --> 00:01:00,369
It's a great opportunity to
get young people to know Tuesla better.

15
00:01:00,369 --> 00:01:02,972
Berry's entering too.

16
00:01:03,989 --> 00:01:06,329
Actually...

17
00:01:06,329 --> 00:01:09,517
I've been thinking about that as well.

18
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:11,209
We're not entering.

19
00:01:11,209 --> 00:01:12,401
What?

20
00:01:12,401 --> 00:01:14,165
Tuesla isn't entering.

21
00:01:17,141 --> 00:01:19,757
I just don't get it.

22
00:01:19,757 --> 00:01:24,400
Do we really need to rank things as above
or below based on our own preferences?

23
00:01:25,309 --> 00:01:28,673
- I understand how you feel, but...
- I won't do that kind of thing.

24
00:01:28,673 --> 00:01:34,517
Maybe I should be the furthest away from
all that win-or-lose stuff.

25
00:01:34,517 --> 00:01:37,725
So, I won't let cuteness be a competition.

26
00:01:37,725 --> 00:01:40,313
- No, but...
- No buts! I don't like it!

27
00:01:40,313 --> 00:01:43,825
Oh, don't be so wishy-washy.

28
00:01:43,825 --> 00:01:47,309
In times like this, just take a quick vote.

29
00:01:47,309 --> 00:01:49,149
[All-Japan Character Grand Prix 2026:
Enter? Don't Enter? Which Will It Be?]

30
00:01:49,149 --> 00:01:52,625
All right, 4 to 1.

31
00:01:52,625 --> 00:01:53,661
According to the voting results,

32
00:01:53,661 --> 00:01:56,945
we've decided to enter
the Character Grand Prix.

33
00:01:56,945 --> 00:01:59,053
4 to 1?

34
00:01:59,941 --> 00:02:03,490
The economic impact of this
Grand Prix grows every year,

35
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:06,249
and just by entering,
a million people will see it.

36
00:02:06,249 --> 00:02:09,689
Exactly! They'll remember
Tuesla's face and name.

37
00:02:09,689 --> 00:02:11,601
To let them know, "Tuesla is right here."

38
00:02:11,601 --> 00:02:14,125
To make our presence known...

39
00:02:14,125 --> 00:02:16,497
Enough!

40
00:02:16,497 --> 00:02:18,689
I thought that you, O-Con, at least...

41
00:02:18,689 --> 00:02:21,708
I thought that you, O-Con, at least,
would understand me!

42
00:02:23,177 --> 00:02:26,423
Hey, Mr. Seo.

43
00:02:31,629 --> 00:02:35,010
He hasn't changed a bit.

44
00:02:35,705 --> 00:02:39,631
He always sulks so easily.

45
00:02:41,277 --> 00:02:46,510
He's been like that ever since he was little.

46
00:02:50,269 --> 00:02:54,023
All right, I'll excuse myself for now.

47
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:02,265
[I've gone on a trip.
Please don't look for me. Mizuki Seo]

48
00:03:10,825 --> 00:03:12,145
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

49
00:03:12,145 --> 00:03:15,249
Running away from home because he's sulking?
Is he a grade-schooler?

50
00:03:15,249 --> 00:03:17,941
He's reading my messages
and ignoring them too.

51
00:03:17,941 --> 00:03:19,817
What?

52
00:03:19,817 --> 00:03:21,089
What is it?

53
00:03:21,089 --> 00:03:24,077
Oh, you know that puppet
I made for promotions?

54
00:03:24,077 --> 00:03:25,585
I can't find it anywhere.

55
00:03:25,585 --> 00:03:27,297
What?

56
00:03:33,073 --> 00:03:36,113
All right, Tuesla, let's go.

57
00:03:44,693 --> 00:03:48,225
[Merry]

58
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:54,897
[32nd Place: Very Good Berry]

59
00:03:55,925 --> 00:04:02,437
If, in this Character Grand Prix,
Berry doesn't place in the top 20,

60
00:04:02,437 --> 00:04:04,717
there won't be any future for her.

61
00:04:04,717 --> 00:04:09,493
So you're just going to discard her? Berry?

62
00:04:09,493 --> 00:04:13,957
We create and sell
what's necessary to match the times.

63
00:04:13,957 --> 00:04:16,777
Am I wrong about that?

64
00:04:16,777 --> 00:04:22,109
To get into the top 20
and prove that Berry is still needed.

65
00:04:22,109 --> 00:04:24,720
That's all you have to do.

66
00:04:39,901 --> 00:04:41,949
For this year's Grand Prix,

67
00:04:41,949 --> 00:04:43,475
[Certificate of Commendation]
our Cynical Molco

68
00:04:43,475 --> 00:04:45,113
[All-Japan Character Grand Prix, 1st Place]
will be taking the top prize.

69
00:04:48,153 --> 00:04:49,867
Excuse me.

70
00:04:50,705 --> 00:04:54,498
Mr. Omishima,
the people from JYC TV are here.

71
00:04:55,181 --> 00:05:00,433
Let's capture the moment
Cynical Molco clinches its third straight win

72
00:05:00,433 --> 00:05:02,913
and is inducted into the Hall of Fame.

73
00:05:02,913 --> 00:05:03,917
[Final Confirmation of Entry Details:
Enter With These Details?]

74
00:05:03,917 --> 00:05:06,213
[Entry Confirmed]
Entry confirmed.

75
00:05:07,801 --> 00:05:10,045
[Entry Characters]

76
00:05:10,045 --> 00:05:15,785
Looking at it again,
it's really quite an impressive lineup.

77
00:05:15,785 --> 00:05:19,230
We'll have to stand out
so we don't get buried in this crowd.

78
00:05:21,009 --> 00:05:25,625
Our next goal is a licensing deal
with a major company.

79
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:30,985
We now need both the voting campaign
and to make a profit as a business.

80
00:05:30,985 --> 00:05:33,365
We need to achieve both at once.

81
00:05:33,365 --> 00:05:36,853
A food or snack manufacturer
would be perfect.

82
00:05:36,853 --> 00:05:40,661
Like chocolates or gummies
that young people and kids love.

83
00:05:40,661 --> 00:05:45,623
Exactly! What we're going for now
is that kind of explosive power,

84
00:05:45,623 --> 00:05:47,788
or rather, viral spread. That's what we want.

85
00:05:52,701 --> 00:05:55,061
Hello, this is Kusakabe.

86
00:05:55,061 --> 00:05:56,825
Yes.

87
00:05:58,029 --> 00:05:59,577
What?

88
00:05:59,577 --> 00:06:01,341
It's here.

89
00:06:06,429 --> 00:06:08,501
Just you watch, O-Con.

90
00:06:08,501 --> 00:06:11,186
I'll do things my way.

91
00:06:22,353 --> 00:06:25,153
[Episode 7]

92
00:06:25,153 --> 00:06:27,185
[Minasawa Beverage Co., Ltd.]
And so, this is

93
00:06:27,185 --> 00:06:31,335
[President and CEO: Yoshio Minasawa]
our new product that will be launching soon.

94
00:06:34,965 --> 00:06:38,929
It's called "Everybody's Cha-Cha-Cha!
Delicious Tea."

95
00:06:38,929 --> 00:06:42,297
"Cha-Cha-Cha Tea" for short.

96
00:06:42,297 --> 00:06:44,581
Cha-Cha-Cha Tea.

97
00:06:44,581 --> 00:06:46,860
Please feel free to give it a try.

98
00:06:47,833 --> 00:06:49,577
I'll enjoy it.

99
00:06:59,217 --> 00:07:01,029
It's delicious.

100
00:07:01,029 --> 00:07:02,485
I really like this.

101
00:07:02,485 --> 00:07:04,245
I'm glad to hear that.

102
00:07:04,245 --> 00:07:07,828
Yes, this is a product we're proud of.

103
00:07:08,465 --> 00:07:12,905
Well, how did you hear about Tuesla?

104
00:07:12,905 --> 00:07:16,168
[Cuteness Changed Our Company!]
I read an article about Mr. Hino

105
00:07:16,168 --> 00:07:19,873
of All Japan Heavy Industries.

106
00:07:19,873 --> 00:07:22,053
- Mr. Hino...
- "Tutu-Tuesla

107
00:07:22,053 --> 00:07:25,413
is just there by my side, supporting me."

108
00:07:25,413 --> 00:07:28,077
"That's what's great about it."

109
00:07:29,093 --> 00:07:34,321
"Just Support"
is this little one's core concept.

110
00:07:34,321 --> 00:07:36,773
Our company feels the exact same way.

111
00:07:36,773 --> 00:07:40,433
On good days and bad days,

112
00:07:40,433 --> 00:07:46,085
we want people to enjoy our
delicious tea that never changes.

113
00:07:46,085 --> 00:07:50,925
We developed this product

114
00:07:50,925 --> 00:07:55,285
to be a tea that can also
support our customers' hearts.

115
00:07:56,081 --> 00:08:00,857
As you can see, we're a small company.

116
00:08:00,857 --> 00:08:04,517
We can't offer the kind of high contract fees
that a major manufacturer can.

117
00:08:04,517 --> 00:08:09,441
So I thought it was presumptuous of me
to even suggest a collaboration.

118
00:08:09,441 --> 00:08:11,170
No, not at all.

119
00:08:11,821 --> 00:08:17,365
But when I first laid eyes on Tuesla here,

120
00:08:18,725 --> 00:08:22,645
I just thought, "Wow, how cute."

121
00:08:22,645 --> 00:08:24,713
It gave me a real jolt.

122
00:08:25,573 --> 00:08:28,855
So, I know I'm being forward here,

123
00:08:28,855 --> 00:08:35,855
but would you be willing to consider
a collaboration with our company?

124
00:08:39,505 --> 00:08:40,649
Compared to a major company,

125
00:08:40,649 --> 00:08:45,725
it's undeniable that the amount
and scale are inevitably smaller.

126
00:08:45,725 --> 00:08:49,593
But the fact that they want to
collaborate with Tuesla

127
00:08:49,593 --> 00:08:51,558
makes me so happy.

128
00:08:52,309 --> 00:08:54,481
- Wait! There he is!
- What?

129
00:08:54,481 --> 00:08:56,273
- There he is!
- What?

130
00:08:58,289 --> 00:09:00,005
<i>I hate you.</i>

131
00:09:01,545 --> 00:09:03,285
<i>I love you.</i>

132
00:09:04,457 --> 00:09:06,355
<i>I hate you.</i>

133
00:09:08,805 --> 00:09:10,561
<i>I love you.</i>

134
00:09:16,157 --> 00:09:18,238
<i>I knew it. I hate you.</i>

135
00:09:18,945 --> 00:09:21,551
<i>I came to a shrine today.</i>

136
00:09:22,201 --> 00:09:24,349
<i>I'm going to go draw a fortune.</i>

137
00:09:26,325 --> 00:09:27,913
<i>Great Curse.</i>

138
00:09:27,913 --> 00:09:32,581
<i>"The one you wait for will not come.
Lost items will not be found."</i>

139
00:09:34,809 --> 00:09:37,356
[What is this? It's terrifying!]
And the comments on it are...

140
00:09:37,356 --> 00:09:38,749
[This came up on my feed, lol.
The poster seems unhinged.]

141
00:09:38,749 --> 00:09:40,929
[It's cute, but so dark...]
I can't believe this.

142
00:09:40,929 --> 00:09:43,445
The designer himself is
destroying the character's world!

143
00:09:43,445 --> 00:09:44,489
[Secret account is here]
And on top of that,

144
00:09:44,489 --> 00:09:45,965
[Officially approved secret account]
if you go to Tuesla's official account,

145
00:09:45,965 --> 00:09:47,153
you can jump right from there to this.

146
00:09:47,153 --> 00:09:49,085
Officially approved secret account?

147
00:09:49,085 --> 00:09:52,677
It's not even a secret anymore at this point.

148
00:09:52,677 --> 00:09:55,529
And he's obviously making sure
that his current location

149
00:09:55,529 --> 00:09:57,607
[Toino]
is visible in the shots.

150
00:10:00,885 --> 00:10:04,517
<i>The number you have dialed is unavailable
at the subscriber's request.</i>

151
00:10:04,517 --> 00:10:06,961
<i>Your call cannot be connected.</i>

152
00:10:06,961 --> 00:10:08,885
Oh, come on!

153
00:10:10,789 --> 00:10:14,105
This is my first time coming here.
I just couldn't resist.

154
00:10:14,105 --> 00:10:17,310
I've got some great news,
and I just couldn't sit still.

155
00:10:18,241 --> 00:10:22,638
They want to use a new character
for this packaging.

156
00:10:24,021 --> 00:10:25,697
[Soft Drink Information]
Elephant Beverages?

157
00:10:25,697 --> 00:10:29,853
Once chosen,
Tuesla's recognition will explode.

158
00:10:29,853 --> 00:10:33,469
They're the biggest player
in the beverage industry.

159
00:10:33,469 --> 00:10:35,633
The licensing fees will be
on a whole other level.

160
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:38,993
Strike while the iron is hot!
You should raise your hand fast.

161
00:10:38,993 --> 00:10:40,893
Chance, chance!

162
00:10:40,893 --> 00:10:44,685
And nice play, me!

163
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:46,409
Thanks.

164
00:11:31,853 --> 00:11:33,862
Could she be lonely?

165
00:11:40,293 --> 00:11:41,893
What?

166
00:11:41,893 --> 00:11:43,641
Oh, you picked up.

167
00:11:45,625 --> 00:11:47,432
What do you want?

168
00:11:48,109 --> 00:11:51,789
It's about work.

169
00:11:51,789 --> 00:11:55,942
<i>Well, I need some advice,
or rather, I have a report for you.</i>

170
00:11:57,021 --> 00:12:00,565
We got a collaboration offer for Tuesla
from a beverage company.

171
00:12:00,565 --> 00:12:02,373
It's not a major one,

172
00:12:02,373 --> 00:12:05,025
but they really connected with
Tuesla's concept,

173
00:12:05,025 --> 00:12:07,589
<i>and they're asking for our help.</i>

174
00:12:07,589 --> 00:12:10,029
<i>However...</i>

175
00:12:10,029 --> 00:12:11,793
However what?

176
00:12:11,793 --> 00:12:13,901
<i>Elephant Beverages, a major company,</i>

177
00:12:13,901 --> 00:12:16,829
<i>also seems to be looking for
a character to collaborate with.</i>

178
00:12:16,829 --> 00:12:21,593
But that one's more like a general call
asking, "Anyone want to collaborate?"

179
00:12:21,593 --> 00:12:24,078
It feels like they're casting a wide net.

180
00:12:24,741 --> 00:12:27,817
But still, a major company
is a major company.

181
00:12:27,817 --> 00:12:32,097
<i>So I'm a bit torn, I guess.</i>

182
00:12:34,697 --> 00:12:38,952
And I was wondering what you would do.

183
00:12:46,253 --> 00:12:50,030
You've already decided, haven't you?

184
00:12:51,829 --> 00:12:55,128
<i>It's fine. Go with whatever
you think is best.</i>

185
00:12:56,565 --> 00:12:59,613
Because I'm probably thinking the same thing.

186
00:13:03,025 --> 00:13:06,973
Okay, thank you very much.

187
00:13:07,925 --> 00:13:09,665
Sure.

188
00:13:10,633 --> 00:13:12,215
So, when are you coming back?

189
00:13:12,215 --> 00:13:15,841
Huh? That's a completely separate issue.

190
00:13:15,841 --> 00:13:18,317
<i>The Grand Prix entry is a separate matter.</i>

191
00:13:52,293 --> 00:13:54,753
Let's do this together.

192
00:13:55,505 --> 00:13:57,385
Really?

193
00:13:57,385 --> 00:14:00,585
If it's with a company
that shares our vision,

194
00:14:00,585 --> 00:14:02,633
I think it will be a wonderful collaboration.

195
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,649
Thank you so much.

196
00:14:04,649 --> 00:14:06,457
Thank you. Please, shake my hand.

197
00:14:06,457 --> 00:14:08,433
- Thank you.
- We look forward to working with you.

198
00:14:08,433 --> 00:14:10,029
Come on, you too.

199
00:14:10,029 --> 00:14:13,873
Today I came to eat a local specialty.

200
00:14:15,929 --> 00:14:20,625
Because emotional wounds can only
be healed by an appetite for good food.

201
00:14:22,189 --> 00:14:24,020
It's so hot!

202
00:14:29,773 --> 00:14:33,613
[Men's Bath]

203
00:14:33,613 --> 00:14:35,520
I'm back to life.

204
00:14:42,929 --> 00:14:49,757
[Arnold and Sylvester]
<i>♪ One day I was struck by lightning ♪</i>

205
00:14:49,757 --> 00:14:57,105
<i>♪ This thrilling spark that came tingling ♪</i>

206
00:14:57,105 --> 00:15:03,825
- <i>♪ Yes ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Yes, this isn't static electricity ♪</i>

207
00:15:03,825 --> 00:15:06,257
- <i>♪ It's love ♪</i>
- <i>♪ It's love ♪</i>

208
00:15:06,257 --> 00:15:11,925
- <i>♪ It was the beginning of love ♪</i>
- Sylvester!

209
00:15:13,153 --> 00:15:14,853
- <i>♪ One day ♪</i>
- What?

210
00:15:14,853 --> 00:15:19,853
- <i>♪ My eyes met yours ♪</i>
- Arnold!

211
00:15:19,853 --> 00:15:24,977
<i>♪ This thrill I want to gaze at forever ♪</i>

212
00:15:24,977 --> 00:15:27,553
What are you doing all the way out here?

213
00:15:27,553 --> 00:15:31,401
What about you? On a trip?

214
00:15:31,401 --> 00:15:34,245
What? I'm here for work.

215
00:15:34,245 --> 00:15:39,969
Like, for input, or maybe output,
at a travel destination.

216
00:15:39,969 --> 00:15:44,830
For me, this is
just a life-sustaining activity.

217
00:15:46,277 --> 00:15:51,615
Arnold and Sylvester are seriously the best!

218
00:15:53,361 --> 00:15:55,865
What's going on? You seem fine.

219
00:15:55,865 --> 00:15:57,705
Huh?

220
00:15:58,369 --> 00:16:02,502
The other day, I was wondering
if something had happened to you.

221
00:16:03,949 --> 00:16:06,877
That was just to check on you.

222
00:16:08,025 --> 00:16:12,221
You've never just shown up like that
at my place before.

223
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:17,033
So, I mean... I thought
maybe something was wrong.

224
00:16:17,033 --> 00:16:21,553
You were worried about me? I'm fine.

225
00:16:23,861 --> 00:16:25,665
Oh, really?

226
00:16:26,929 --> 00:16:32,478
How many years has it been
since we talked like this?

227
00:16:34,061 --> 00:16:38,113
Since I left Merry, I don't think
we've spoken even once.

228
00:16:42,353 --> 00:16:44,170
Back then...

229
00:17:05,317 --> 00:17:08,320
why didn't you say anything?

230
00:17:09,441 --> 00:17:12,498
It was your decision, Mi.

231
00:17:14,297 --> 00:17:17,965
What the designer Mizuki Seo decides,

232
00:17:17,965 --> 00:17:22,141
it's not my place to interfere.

233
00:17:22,857 --> 00:17:29,189
But it's tough working alone.

234
00:17:29,189 --> 00:17:31,773
I sometimes thought about

235
00:17:31,773 --> 00:17:38,297
asking you to come back to Merry,
if you were up for it.

236
00:17:39,985 --> 00:17:41,733
But...

237
00:17:42,737 --> 00:17:44,928
you're doing so well on your own.

238
00:17:46,649 --> 00:17:52,285
Mi, do you ever regret it? Leaving Merry?

239
00:17:54,409 --> 00:17:56,658
No, I don't regret it, not even for a second.

240
00:17:58,181 --> 00:18:02,408
And I'm not alone now.

241
00:18:04,301 --> 00:18:06,125
I see.

242
00:18:09,213 --> 00:18:10,841
Well, see you.

243
00:18:10,841 --> 00:18:11,845
Huh?

244
00:18:11,845 --> 00:18:14,349
I'm busy.

245
00:18:14,349 --> 00:18:16,213
It's about the Character Grand Prix.

246
00:18:16,213 --> 00:18:21,153
I have to get Berry into the rankings.

247
00:18:22,165 --> 00:18:29,127
If that doesn't happen, then I'm done too.

248
00:18:29,945 --> 00:18:32,193
See you, Mi.

249
00:18:37,777 --> 00:18:40,053
- Hey, the confetti didn't make it
- Yes.

250
00:18:40,053 --> 00:18:42,077
- in time for the start of the song.
- I'm sorry.

251
00:18:42,077 --> 00:18:43,945
- You need to think about the distance.
- Yes.

252
00:18:43,945 --> 00:18:46,073
The responsibility is mine.

253
00:18:46,073 --> 00:18:47,777
I'm sorry.

254
00:18:47,777 --> 00:18:51,049
- What? Mr. Seo?
- Mugi.

255
00:18:51,049 --> 00:18:52,321
What?

256
00:18:52,321 --> 00:18:55,446
Who's this? A friend of yours?

257
00:18:56,673 --> 00:18:58,785
- No, I don't know him.
- Mugi!

258
00:18:58,785 --> 00:19:02,381
- Mom can join too, if you'd like.
- Please take one.

259
00:19:02,381 --> 00:19:06,795
Wouldn't it be nice
if you voted for Cynical Molco? Hmph.

260
00:19:07,425 --> 00:19:11,370
Isn't handing those out a violation
of the Public Offices Election Act?

261
00:19:14,061 --> 00:19:16,481
[Here is the data for the collaboration
design. Please review it. Thank you!]

262
00:19:16,481 --> 00:19:19,093
Mr. Seo gave the okay
on the collaboration design.

263
00:19:19,093 --> 00:19:22,865
He replies to work stuff,
but completely ignores everything else.

264
00:19:22,865 --> 00:19:25,313
He's so immature.

265
00:19:25,313 --> 00:19:27,393
Sorry for the wait!

266
00:19:28,405 --> 00:19:30,305
Oh, my!

267
00:19:30,305 --> 00:19:32,953
Is your back okay?

268
00:19:32,953 --> 00:19:37,973
Totally fine! My back
feels like a rising dragon!

269
00:19:39,481 --> 00:19:42,929
All right! We also can't afford to lose here.

270
00:19:42,929 --> 00:19:44,857
Let's do this!

271
00:19:44,857 --> 00:19:48,582
- We're Tutu-Tuesla!
- Nice to meet you!

272
00:19:48,582 --> 00:19:50,769
- Thanks.
- I know!

273
00:19:50,769 --> 00:19:51,869
It's popular with middle-aged men, right?

274
00:19:51,869 --> 00:19:54,133
- Yeah, my dad likes it too.
- Cute!

275
00:19:54,133 --> 00:19:55,133
Cute!

276
00:19:55,133 --> 00:19:58,681
New merch is on sale now! Tutu-Tuesla!

277
00:19:58,681 --> 00:20:03,889
We're Tutu-Tuesla! Thank you!

278
00:20:03,889 --> 00:20:06,533
Please increase Molco's media exposure.

279
00:20:06,533 --> 00:20:08,349
Hurry up with the plan.

280
00:20:08,349 --> 00:20:11,733
- Yes, sir.
- Well, excuse me.

281
00:20:11,733 --> 00:20:14,017
Where's Ms. Mondo?

282
00:20:14,017 --> 00:20:18,365
She's working hard to
try to raise Berry's ranking.

283
00:20:18,365 --> 00:20:20,285
All by herself.

284
00:20:20,285 --> 00:20:22,661
- So cute.
- I'm glad.

285
00:20:22,661 --> 00:20:27,213
[Berry Signing Event]

286
00:20:27,213 --> 00:20:29,141
Hello.

287
00:20:29,141 --> 00:20:33,929
Do you know Berry?

288
00:20:33,929 --> 00:20:35,633
Yes, I know her.

289
00:20:36,893 --> 00:20:38,741
My grandma gave her to me.

290
00:20:38,741 --> 00:20:42,561
My friends all say she's not cool anymore,

291
00:20:42,561 --> 00:20:47,357
but I really like Berry.

292
00:20:47,357 --> 00:20:49,505
Thank you.

293
00:20:59,081 --> 00:21:00,861
Amazing!

294
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:08,249
Is there another pose you'd like me to draw?

295
00:21:09,269 --> 00:21:11,585
What? Really?

296
00:21:11,585 --> 00:21:14,977
As a special bonus service!

297
00:21:14,977 --> 00:21:16,801
Yay!

298
00:21:16,801 --> 00:21:20,981
Then I want one where she's giving a kiss.

299
00:21:20,981 --> 00:21:22,901
Nice choice.

300
00:21:22,901 --> 00:21:25,297
That'll be so cute!

301
00:21:29,557 --> 00:21:31,981
[Cha-Cha-Cha]

302
00:21:31,981 --> 00:21:35,551
Awesome! It looks adorable!

303
00:21:37,965 --> 00:21:40,429
[Original Stickers: 8 types]

304
00:21:45,761 --> 00:21:49,411
[Thanks for confirming]

305
00:21:49,411 --> 00:21:53,061
[When are you coming back, Mr. Seo?]

306
00:21:53,061 --> 00:21:55,370
So you reply to this kind of thing?

307
00:21:57,229 --> 00:21:59,088
Oh, it's Tuesla.

308
00:22:01,093 --> 00:22:03,956
Oh. Oh, nice.

309
00:22:09,145 --> 00:22:12,845
Thank you, mister.

310
00:22:12,845 --> 00:22:15,005
Daddy, I want this one.

311
00:22:15,005 --> 00:22:17,417
Huh? This is the one we usually get.

312
00:22:17,417 --> 00:22:20,813
I want this one. It's cuter.

313
00:22:20,813 --> 00:22:22,753
- Thanks.
- Go ahead, pick one.

314
00:22:22,753 --> 00:22:26,633
Thanks, son.

315
00:22:26,633 --> 00:22:28,609
Oh, isn't this the one

316
00:22:28,609 --> 00:22:30,925
- that's been popping up a lot recently?
- Yeah, I know it.

317
00:22:30,925 --> 00:22:32,261
Tutu-Tuesla, right?

318
00:22:32,261 --> 00:22:35,245
- The one doing the flower fortune-telling.
- Yeah.

319
00:22:35,245 --> 00:22:39,485
- Surprisingly cute, right?
- Totally!

320
00:22:40,493 --> 00:22:42,053
[29,085 followers]
It's growing.

321
00:22:42,053 --> 00:22:45,529
It was right around when Mr. Seo
started posting those surreal videos.

322
00:22:45,529 --> 00:22:48,001
They do have this weird,
addictive quality about them.

323
00:22:48,001 --> 00:22:50,721
It's like a hybrid of cute and surreal.

324
00:22:50,721 --> 00:22:53,473
Look at the view count!

325
00:22:53,473 --> 00:22:55,898
500,000 views?

326
00:22:57,561 --> 00:23:00,477
"This video came up
right when I got dumped by my boyfriend."

327
00:23:00,477 --> 00:23:04,255
"I felt like it was grieving with me."

328
00:23:06,549 --> 00:23:10,061
Oh, today's post is up.

329
00:23:10,061 --> 00:23:13,619
- <i>♪ Wherever I am ♪</i>
- Huh?

330
00:23:13,619 --> 00:23:17,109
- <i>♪ I think of you ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Of muscles ♪</i>

331
00:23:17,109 --> 00:23:20,065
- <i>♪ Love, this is love, this is love ♪</i>
- Come on!

332
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:26,621
<i>♪ This is love, love, love... ♪</i>

333
00:23:26,621 --> 00:23:28,513
[Muscle Idols, Arnold and Sylvester]
You really didn't have to help out, though.

334
00:23:28,513 --> 00:23:32,157
Well... but you let us film that video.

335
00:23:32,157 --> 00:23:33,481
Thanks.

336
00:23:33,481 --> 00:23:37,001
Big bros seem really happy
to be collaborating with Tuesla.

337
00:23:37,001 --> 00:23:39,901
It has a real fanbase among middle-aged guys.

338
00:23:41,413 --> 00:23:43,213
Are you okay?

339
00:23:43,213 --> 00:23:45,989
So? Who are those guys?

340
00:23:45,989 --> 00:23:48,873
Oh, they're fellow disciples, like me.

341
00:23:49,777 --> 00:23:52,481
- There are others?
- Yes.

342
00:23:52,481 --> 00:23:54,809
If we want to be able to
stand on that stage someday,

343
00:23:54,809 --> 00:23:56,618
we've got to work hard now.

344
00:24:07,537 --> 00:24:09,337
Oh! That's heavy! What is this?

345
00:24:09,337 --> 00:24:11,573
Oh, these are custom-made folding chairs.

346
00:24:11,573 --> 00:24:13,393
Each of them weighs 10 kilograms.

347
00:24:13,393 --> 00:24:16,381
Venue setup and strength training in one go.

348
00:24:16,381 --> 00:24:19,886
We're competing to see
who can put away the most.

349
00:24:32,293 --> 00:24:36,117
You guys have it rough,
being forced to compete.

350
00:24:36,117 --> 00:24:38,157
It's not like that.

351
00:24:38,157 --> 00:24:40,253
Because we're...

352
00:24:40,253 --> 00:24:42,218
We're honing our skills together.

353
00:24:42,845 --> 00:24:47,076
We're rivals, but also fellow dream-chasers.

354
00:24:47,821 --> 00:24:49,281
Yes!

355
00:24:49,281 --> 00:24:51,413
What are you doing? We're leaving! Hurry up!

356
00:24:51,413 --> 00:24:52,709
Okay, Adrianne!

357
00:24:52,709 --> 00:24:54,573
I'll be back!

358
00:24:57,133 --> 00:25:00,039
[Muscle Idols, Arnold and Sylvester]

359
00:25:01,749 --> 00:25:04,033
Honing skills together?

360
00:25:06,945 --> 00:25:08,717
Hey, that's...

361
00:25:10,361 --> 00:25:12,581
It's Tuesla. Do you know it?

362
00:25:12,581 --> 00:25:15,273
No, no, it's not about knowing it.

363
00:25:15,273 --> 00:25:16,557
Do you like it? Tuesla?

364
00:25:16,557 --> 00:25:19,418
Yeah, I like it. It's cute, isn't it?

365
00:25:23,537 --> 00:25:25,001
Hang on a sec.

366
00:25:25,001 --> 00:25:27,493
[Cha-Cha-Cha, Original Stickers, 8 types]

367
00:25:27,493 --> 00:25:29,873
Here we go.

368
00:25:29,873 --> 00:25:33,137
- And then like this.
- Is he drawing something?

369
00:25:33,137 --> 00:25:36,285
- What's this?
- And then like this.

370
00:25:36,285 --> 00:25:37,541
What are you doing?

371
00:25:37,541 --> 00:25:39,433
- What are you drawing?
- What's this?

372
00:25:39,433 --> 00:25:42,073
- Watch.
- What's this?

373
00:25:42,073 --> 00:25:43,997
All done!

374
00:25:43,997 --> 00:25:45,313
- Tuesla!
- It's Tuesla!

375
00:25:45,313 --> 00:25:46,981
- Awesome!
- It's Tuesla!

376
00:25:46,981 --> 00:25:48,225
- Tuesla.
- So cool.

377
00:25:48,225 --> 00:25:49,781
It's Tutu-Tuesla.

378
00:25:49,781 --> 00:25:52,385
- Tutu-Tuesla.
- Tuesla.

379
00:25:53,617 --> 00:25:54,903
[Ms. Mondo]
Please do your best.

380
00:25:54,903 --> 00:25:56,769
[Berry Signing Event]
Thank you very much.

381
00:26:04,795 --> 00:26:07,761
This is a special tea
done in collaboration with Tuesla.

382
00:26:07,761 --> 00:26:11,645
Hello! If it's all right with you,
please vote for Tuesla.

383
00:26:11,645 --> 00:26:13,101
Thank you.

384
00:26:13,101 --> 00:26:16,381
Thanks to you, sales are going strong.

385
00:26:17,685 --> 00:26:20,085
It's all because Tuesla supported us.

386
00:26:20,085 --> 00:26:21,494
- Thank you.
- No, not at all...

387
00:26:21,494 --> 00:26:24,738
I should be thanking you. Thank you.

388
00:26:25,381 --> 00:26:27,692
- Tea in collaboration with Tuesla.
- Nice.

389
00:26:27,692 --> 00:26:30,028
- Thank you.
- Its ears...

390
00:26:31,513 --> 00:26:34,401
- Give it a squeeze.
- It's a special tea.

391
00:26:34,401 --> 00:26:36,077
- The ribbon! The ribbon!
- If it's all right with you,

392
00:26:36,077 --> 00:26:38,647
- please vote for Tuesla.
- So cute.

393
00:26:38,647 --> 00:26:40,509
- Thank you.
- Give it a squeeze.

394
00:26:52,249 --> 00:26:55,937
